  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mobile Cinema: East of Noon Screenings in the Delta &amp; Upper Egypt 2025 - 2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&apos;East of Noon&apos; is a Dutch-Egyptian-Qatari feature film with the Netherlands as the majority production partner. Shot entirely on 16 mm film, it marks the first Egyptian film made in this format since 1988. In order to achieve this, the film crew undertook a restoration of the film laboratory in Cairo which was closed for over ten years. 

While Cairo and Alexandria traditionally dominate Egypt&apos;s cultural landscape, many cities across the country still lack access to cinemas and other cultural venues. With &apos;East of Noon&apos; the team aims to bring cinema to new audiences, particularly young people interested in filmmaking, by organizing a series of screenings and discussions with the director and film crew in various cities throughout the Delta and Upper Egypt. 

Through this initiative, the NL Embassy in Cairo will boost the NL cultural &amp; film sector, while strengthening Dutch-Egyptian cultural collaboration.</narrative>
  </description>
